+## Durable artifacts (authoritative)
 
-A completion-toggle state change rebuilds the list (`todoList.innerHTML = ...` or an unconditional
-`renderList()`), detaching and recreating the `<li>` nodes. A browser (Cypress) that holds a reference
-to an `<li>` before the click sees the old node detach, so a chained `cy.find()` fails. The fix is
-app-side: mutate the existing node in place (toggle its `completed` class and the checkbox `.checked`)
-when the item stays visible under the current filter, so the node stays attached across the interaction.
